## Frontend Defaults

[% if frontend_apps | length > 0 -%]
Configured web apps:

[% for app in frontend_apps -%]
- `<<[ app.name ]>>` in `<<[ app.dir ]>>`
[% endfor %]

Each configured app is expected to support `lint`, `typecheck`, `build:bundle`, and `test:coverage`.
Structured work uses four atomic path-aware gates per app; repository-wide TypeScript checks remain available for an intentional full-matrix run.
[% if application_contracts_enabled -%]
Application contract freshness and public deployment boundaries have separate `application-contracts` and `public-artifacts` work gates; `jig-contract` remains limited to Jig harness wiring.
[% endif -%]
`test:coverage` must write `coverage/coverage-summary.json` in the app directory for threshold enforcement.
Run package-local scripts through `scripts/check-webapps.sh run-script <app-dir> <script>` so the configured app and required script are selected consistently. Preserve repository-owned registry, authentication, dependency, and lifecycle policy.
`[[frontend_apps]]` defines CI and coverage; `[dev]` and `[[dev.apps]]` define local development. Each frontend app needs a matching dev app name and directory. Extra dev-only apps are outside generated web CI; remove legacy `dev_command` keys.
[% else -%]
No web apps are configured in `.jig.toml`.
[% endif %]

